{"description":"sto:compliance-telemetry (M5) asks for a report of, per repository and period: sessions observed; sessions that retrieved a constraint before their first write; gate failures; violations repaired within the same session — and its acceptance criterion 2 forbids inventing new capture fields. Recon shows none of the four numbers is derivable from data EKA stores today. (1) No session concept exists: `sessionId` appears nowhere in eka-core, eka-cli or eka-standard schemas; the store has no session/event/audit table (tables: projects, repos, object_refs, object_payloads, attachments, meta, sync_log). (2) No retrieval is recorded: reads (`eka get`/`context`, MCP reads) are stateless and unlogged, so 'read a binding before the first write' has no source. (3) Gate failures are not persisted: transition refusals are returned to the caller and discarded; no refusal row is written. (4) 'Repaired within the same session' needs both a session key and a failure record, so it inherits (1) and (3). What capture DOES persist (spec:provenance-capture, ADR-035 v3) is provenance (human|inferred|reconciled), sourcePromptHash, confidence, sourceCommitSha and captureMeta (classifier, dedupeKey, title). There is also a direct conflict with the design: research-LLM-context-efficiency.md rejects session state on the server ('No server session state in EKA'; 'Reject = EKA maintaining per-agent session table'), so adding a session key to satisfy M5 would contradict an accepted finding.","impact":"M5 cannot be implemented against existing data without either (a) inventing capture fields M5 itself disallows, or (b) introducing a session/retrieval/gate-failure log that the accepted research rejects. Illegitimate shortcuts (deriving a fake 'session' from timestamp adjacency or counting workflow transitions as 'gate failures') would produce numbers that look like the requested metric while measuring something else — exactly the 'claim without a number' failure M5 says it exists to prevent. M5 must be redefined to a metric that is honestly derivable from stored provenance, or an upstream work item (a capture/session-log design) must land first."}